  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1204.50 Topcoat",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1204.50 \"Topcoat\" means the final coating system applied to provide the final color or protective finish, or both. The term includes a monocoat color or basecoat/clearcoat system, in-line repair, and 2-tone coatings, and includes other coating(s), such as blackout or interior color, applied in the same spray booth(s).\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1200.html"
}
